WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.901
-This is how it works.

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:02.902
In front of each of us
are two envelopes

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:03.970
containing confessions.

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.438
One is true,
and the other is a lie.

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:06.672
Once you read the confession,

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:08.441
the two other players
get to interrogate you.

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:10.577
They have to come
to a unanimous decision --

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:14.213
is it the truth,
or it the lie?

00:00:14.213 --> 00:00:15.314
Billie, you'll go first.

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:17.083
Colin, which envelope
should she open?

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:19.518
-Mm.
Uh, 2.

00:00:19.518 --> 00:00:21.754
-Mm. Mm-hmm.
-This?

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:24.391
-Numero dos.

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:26.359
-Wait.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:28.127
-Can you open an envelope?
-Shut up.

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:29.395
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:31.397
Oh, it's open on the bottom.
-Yeah.

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:32.665
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:33.966
-Okay.
Are you ready for this?

00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:35.301
-Okay. All right.

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:38.271
That is a strong...
-Strong fake cigarette.

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:42.275
-Um...
So, I once farted

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:45.845
in my friend's mouth while she
was yawning, and she threw up.

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:48.214
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.549
-Wait.
What year was this?

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:53.086
♪♪

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:55.688
-Um, it was, um...

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:59.659
I was 12, so it was --
-Last year?

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:00.927
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:01.928
So it was last year.
Okay, great.

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:04.096
-It was 2014.
-Okay.

00:01:04.096 --> 00:01:05.364
-I was 12.
-And where were you?

00:01:05.364 --> 00:01:07.667
-I was in my yard.
-Out back, in your backyard?

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.702
-Yeah, my backyard.
In my backyard.

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:11.537
-Daytime?
-Yeah.

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:13.339
-No, they were at nighttime
in the backyard.

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:14.674
What are you --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:16.776
Do you think it's camping?
-Yeah.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:17.977
-What were you doing?
Like, wrestling

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:19.879
or fooling around
or doing gymnastics?

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.513
-Whoa.
-I was -- So, I was --

00:01:21.513 --> 00:01:24.683
It was like, there was a table,
and she was sitting.

00:01:24.683 --> 00:01:25.952
-Oh, please.
-I was standing here.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.387
So, she was sitting, like,
facing this way.

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:28.954
I was standing here,
facing that way.

00:01:28.954 --> 00:01:30.389
-Okay.
-She was eating.

00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:31.724
-And where's the table?

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:34.193
-The table's here, so she was
facing the other way.

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:35.328
-Okay.
-What was she eating?

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:36.529
-Pizza.
-Pizza.

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:39.064
-Daytime pizza.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.064 --> 00:01:40.566
-You want some nighttime pizza?
Like...

00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:42.468
-That's kind of --
All right.

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:43.669
Kind of running
out of time here.

00:01:43.669 --> 00:01:45.939
I don't know.
We need to ask more questions.

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:48.074
And are you friends
with her today?

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:50.409
-Ye-- Sort of.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:52.178
-Was it weird after that?

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:54.813
-It was so funny.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:54.813 --> 00:01:56.215
-So funny.
-What do you think?

00:01:56.215 --> 00:01:59.318
I think...
-I think...true.

00:01:59.318 --> 00:02:00.486
-Yeah, I think true.
I think it sounds

00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:02.822
like something weirdly --
-It sucks.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:05.591
-Is it true?
-Yes.

00:02:05.591 --> 00:02:08.595
♪♪

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:10.997
-Oh, my God.

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:13.232
But why did you do that?
Did you do that --

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:14.600
Why did you do that?
Was it on purpose?

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.402
-It was silent.
Listen, it was silent.

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.704
I did not think it would be bad,
but, you know,

00:02:18.704 --> 00:02:21.474
those are always the worst ones.
-Okay, here we go.

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:23.776
-That's the problem.
-Which envelope should I open?

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:25.444
Truth or lie?
What do you think?

00:02:25.444 --> 00:02:28.247
Billie?
Colin?

00:02:28.247 --> 00:02:30.416
-Uh...one.
-Yeah.

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.285
-Doesn't matter
because I'm such a good actor.

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:36.155
-Well...
Whoa.

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:38.358
-Shut up.
-Ever see a movie called "Taxi"?

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:40.893
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:42.594
-Okay, here we go.

00:02:42.594 --> 00:02:44.964
Oh, I got fired from my job
at the supermarket

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:46.532
for pretending to be French.

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:49.902
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:52.271
-When?
-This is -- I was 15,

00:02:52.271 --> 00:02:53.406
so I'd probably say --

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:55.475
-What was the name
of the supermarket?

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:57.810
-Oddly, it was Great American
was the name of the supermarket.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.479
-Can you repeat?
What happened?

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:03.215
-I got fired from my job
for pretending to be French.

00:03:03.215 --> 00:03:04.617
-Why were you
pretending to be French?

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:06.152
-I was bored.
-You were bored.

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:07.520
-I was bored.
I was putting stickers

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.456
on canned -- canned foods.
I was bored.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:11.524
And people
would ask me questions,

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:15.028
and I'd be like, "Non."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:17.196
"Non." And then, sometimes
people would ask for something,

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:18.898
I'd go, "You want --"

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:20.833
And I would point
to French dressing.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:22.268
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:25.304
Or if it was around mustard, I
would point to French's mustard.

00:03:25.304 --> 00:03:27.039
And I think
someone ratted on me.

00:03:27.039 --> 00:03:29.074
Someone complained, and then
they said, "Who did it?"

00:03:29.074 --> 00:03:30.309
And then one of my friends
ratted on me.

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:32.044
-The French guy, yeah?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:32.044 --> 00:03:34.147
"Who was pretending to be French
and not helping people?"

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:35.481
-And then I was like,
"I don't know who."

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:37.550
-Sound like a very pretentious
15-year-old, by the way.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:38.851
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.786
-So, you're pretending
to not understand them.

00:03:40.786 --> 00:03:43.189
-"I don't know.
I don't know."

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:45.091
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:46.158
-You were 15.
-Yeah.

00:03:46.158 --> 00:03:47.259
♪♪

00:03:47.259 --> 00:03:49.495
All right.
What do you guys think?

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:54.100
-Uh...

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.769
-I don't think so.

00:03:56.769 --> 00:04:00.172
-Mnh-mnh.
I want to say...

00:04:00.172 --> 00:04:02.308
It's almost, like,
not funny enough to be true.

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:04.276
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.276 --> 00:04:06.011
-Now, you -- Now I'm thinking --
-Like, you know what I'm saying?

00:04:06.011 --> 00:04:08.247
Like, we agree?
-Now I'm thinking it did happen.

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:10.582
-You know what I'm saying?
[ Sad trombone ]

00:04:10.582 --> 00:04:12.352
-Now you're thinking
it did happen because --

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:14.019
-I'm just gonna say it happened.

00:04:14.019 --> 00:04:15.721
You can say it didn't
so one of us can win.

00:04:15.721 --> 00:04:17.056
-Okay, good.
-Okay?

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:18.224
-No, I think
you have to be unanimous.

00:04:18.224 --> 00:04:20.859
-No, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.859 --> 00:04:22.494
-I like how you're just
playing this game, he goes,

00:04:22.494 --> 00:04:23.863
"No, I think you have to be --"

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:24.997
You don't even know the rules
of your game.

00:04:24.997 --> 00:04:27.166
[ Laughter ]
-You have to be unanimous.

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:28.968
Ready?
1, 2, 3 -- yea or nay?

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.436
-Yea.
-Yea.

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:32.237
-You think yea, it did happen.
-I think it did happen.

00:04:32.237 --> 00:04:33.873
-Yeah.
It did not happen.

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:35.874
-Oh!
-You were right!

00:04:35.874 --> 00:04:37.443
You should've stuck
to your guess!

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:40.012
That's the lesson learned --
stick to your guess.

00:04:40.012 --> 00:04:41.246
No.

00:04:41.246 --> 00:04:44.049
I did get fired
but it was for doing whip-its.

00:04:44.049 --> 00:04:45.818
Colin, I think you should --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:46.953
You should --
I think you should go.

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:48.754
-Come on, baby.
-I think number one.

00:04:48.754 --> 00:04:50.122
'Cause you know why?
You're number one to me, man.

00:04:50.122 --> 00:04:52.325
-Aw, thanks.
-Yeah.

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:53.859
Here we go.
-Okay. Ready?

00:04:53.859 --> 00:04:56.395
-Yeah.
-My first stand-up set

00:04:56.395 --> 00:04:59.765
was in a police station
while I was under arrest.

00:04:59.765 --> 00:05:01.934
-That's so cool.
-This is absolutely true.

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:04.069
This is so true.
-I love --

00:05:04.069 --> 00:05:06.471
-He's Colin Quinn.
He's the most Irish guy I know.

00:05:06.471 --> 00:05:09.274
This is perfect for his
one-man show and first book.

00:05:09.274 --> 00:05:10.343
This is so him.

00:05:10.343 --> 00:05:12.411
He did stand-up
in a police station.

00:05:12.411 --> 00:05:14.447
Why were you arrested?

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:16.482
-Possession of
a controlled substance.

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:18.384
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:20.286
-So, you had weed on you,
or was it something else?

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:21.420
-[ Laughs ]
-Yeah, you don't want to say.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:24.356
[ Laughter ]

00:05:24.356 --> 00:05:25.658
-Wait.
But how old were you?

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:26.959
-You get arrested for weed?
Come on.

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:28.461
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:30.996
-How old were you?
-Uh, 22.

00:05:30.996 --> 00:05:32.898
-Oh, my gosh.
He totally did this.

00:05:32.898 --> 00:05:36.469
It was you-know-what and the
thing, and he got busted.

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:38.036
Were you in a car
or something, driving?

00:05:38.036 --> 00:05:39.538
-No.
-That's right, because you

00:05:39.538 --> 00:05:41.107
grew up in the streets
of Brooklyn,

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:42.441
and that's
how you have your accent.

00:05:42.441 --> 00:05:44.009
So you were walking around,
you started some trouble.

00:05:44.009 --> 00:05:45.978
-I just like picturing it.

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:47.312
-You got in a fight
with somebody?

00:05:47.312 --> 00:05:49.915
-No.
-How did you get arrested?

00:05:49.915 --> 00:05:51.117
-What is that?
-How did you get arrested?

00:05:51.117 --> 00:05:53.653
You were buying?
-Possession -- 'Cause I was --

00:05:53.653 --> 00:05:56.021
-The whole way
on Fifth Avenue and 43rd Street.

00:05:56.021 --> 00:05:58.091
-How much cocaine did you have?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.091 --> 00:06:00.393
-It was fake.
-It was fake cocaine?

00:06:00.393 --> 00:06:02.495
-It was fake.
Don't do fake cocaine.

00:06:02.495 --> 00:06:04.463
[ Laughter ]
I love it.

00:06:04.463 --> 00:06:06.432
-You're not a role model
for children.

00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:08.033
"Don't do fake cocaine."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:12.872
Don't do cocaine at all!
Real or fake.

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:15.507
-What's fake cocaine?
-I know him pretty well.

00:06:15.507 --> 00:06:17.743
-Called procaine.
-Procaine.

00:06:17.743 --> 00:06:19.578
-That's what they called it!

00:06:19.578 --> 00:06:21.680
-I think of course
this happened to him,

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:24.750
'cause he has this type of luck.
-I just love to picture it.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:26.318
So I'm gonna -- I feel like
it's true, you know?

00:06:26.318 --> 00:06:27.786
-Gosh, if he's lying,
you're a genius,

00:06:27.786 --> 00:06:29.555
'cause he is a good actor, too.
I'm gonna say it's true.

00:06:29.555 --> 00:06:31.123
-I think it's true.

00:06:31.123 --> 00:06:32.491
-It's true.
-Yeah!

00:06:32.491 --> 00:06:36.061
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:36.061 --> 00:06:38.464
Come on.
I love you, buddy.

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:40.099
Oh, there's
the truth right there!

00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:42.402
Billie Eilish, Colin Quinn,
everybody!

